# chip_tracks, with MIRROR-SYMMETRIC HORIZONTAL patterns.
#
# Same stack as chip_tracks.buda (M2..M11), same layer widths, same signal
# counts, same periods and therefore the SAME 504 placement grid and the same
# overhead percentages.  The only change is where the WHITESPACE sits on the
# four H layers, plus a few-unit shift of three H origins.
#
# WHY.  A flipped instance's routing is its reference's routing reflected
# about the instance's own centreline.  For the copy to land on real tracks
# the layer's pattern must be invariant under that reflection, i.e. the
# centreline must fall on a reflection axis of the pattern.  In chip_tracks
# the H patterns have NO reflection axis at all: each rail carries a WIDER
# GAP AFTER IT THAN BEFORE IT (M2/M4: 1 after, 0.5 before), so the unit is
# not a palindrome and no axis exists at any offset.  M6 is the exception —
# its gaps are 1 on both sides — and it is the only H layer in chip_tracks
# that does have an axis.
#
# THE FIX is to centre each rail in its own whitespace: give the signal that
# PRECEDES a rail the same space_after as the rail itself.  Written per layer
# as `... SIGNAL w g  POWER rail g ...`, the unit becomes a palindrome and
# gains axes every half period.  The gap g is then solved to keep the period
# unchanged (period/2 = rail + 2g + n*sig + (n-1)*s), which is what preserves
# the 504 grid, the bit pitches and the overheads:
#
#   layer  period  rail  sig  s     g      axis (mod p/2)
#   M2/M4    18     2     1   0.5   0.75   1
#   M6       24     3     1   1     1      1.5   (already symmetric)
#   M8       56     8     3   1.5   1.75   4
#   M10      74    10     4   2     2.5    5
#
# ORIGINS.  Symmetry creates the axes; the origin decides WHERE they land.
# The condition is  instance_centre - origin == axis  (mod period/2).  The
# three flipped instances of chip_stack sit at centres 8694 / 10710 / 12222,
# which differ by multiples of 504, so ONE origin per layer serves all three.
# M2's origin already satisfied it; M4/M6/M8 are shifted by 1 / 3.5 / 2 units.
#
# M10 CANNOT be satisfied and does not need to be: its half period 37 does not
# divide 504, so the three flipped centres fall on three different residues.
# That is precisely why `reserve_top_layers 2` caps cells at M9 — the grid is
# the LCM over the layers the CELLS use, and M10 is not one of them.  It is
# made symmetric here only so the stack is uniform.
#
# The V layers (M3/M5/M7/M9/M11) are untouched: an upside-down flip maps
# y -> 2d-y and leaves x alone, so vertical tracks are unaffected by it.
def_layer  2 M2  H LOW 55.56
def_layer  3 M3  V LOW 55.56
def_layer  4 M4  H TOP 55.56
def_layer  5 M5  V TOP 55.56
def_layer  6 M6  H TOP 66.67
def_layer  7 M7  V TOP 58.97
def_layer  8 M8  H TOP 57.14
def_layer  9 M9  V TOP 57.14
def_layer 10 M10 H TOP 56.76
def_layer 11 M11 V TOP 56.76

# H layers — symmetric units (rail centred in its gap), periods unchanged.
def_track_pattern 2  -100   POWER 2 0.75  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.75  GROUND 2 0.75  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.75
def_track_pattern 4  -199   POWER 2 0.75  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.75  GROUND 2 0.75  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.75
def_track_pattern 6  -403.5 POWER 3 1     SIGNAL 1 1    SIGNAL 1 1    SIGNAL 1 1    SIGNAL 1 1     GROUND 3 1     SIGNAL 1 1    SIGNAL 1 1    SIGNAL 1 1    SIGNAL 1 1
def_track_pattern 8  -802   POWER 8 1.75  SIGNAL 3 1.5  SIGNAL 3 1.5  SIGNAL 3 1.5  SIGNAL 3 1.75  GROUND 8 1.75  SIGNAL 3 1.5  SIGNAL 3 1.5  SIGNAL 3 1.5  SIGNAL 3 1.75
def_track_pattern 10 -1200  POWER 10 2.5  SIGNAL 4 2    SIGNAL 4 2    SIGNAL 4 2    SIGNAL 4 2.5   GROUND 10 2.5  SIGNAL 4 2    SIGNAL 4 2    SIGNAL 4 2    SIGNAL 4 2.5

# V layers — unchanged from chip_tracks.buda (a y-flip does not move them).
def_track_pattern 3     0  POWER 2 1  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  GROUND 2 1  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5
def_track_pattern 5     0  POWER 2 1  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  GROUND 2 1  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5
def_track_pattern 7  -600  POWER 6 2  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1  GROUND 6 1  SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1
def_track_pattern 9 -1000  POWER 8 2  SIGNAL 3 1.5  SIGNAL 3 1.5  SIGNAL 3 1.5  SIGNAL 3 1.5  GROUND 8 2  SIGNAL 3 1.5  SIGNAL 3 1.5  SIGNAL 3 1.5  SIGNAL 3 1.5
def_track_pattern 11 -1400 POWER 10 3  SIGNAL 4 2  SIGNAL 4 2  SIGNAL 4 2  SIGNAL 4 2  GROUND 10 3  SIGNAL 4 2  SIGNAL 4 2  SIGNAL 4 2  SIGNAL 4 2

report_overhead
